# Target C — interface / augmented-defect dichotomy

**Date:** 2026-09-12  
**Lifecycle:** audited-working route module; theorem-state authority unchanged.  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** **STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.**

This module normalizes the independently audited content of the former proof-only
“Section 127” branch without reusing a section number.

Use canonical Section-123 augmented-cell quantities

\[
A_*:=\sum_r(a_r-T_r),
\qquad
Q_*:=\sum_rQ_r^+,
\qquad
J_{\rm aug}:=A_*+Q_*+2d_{\rm tile}.
\]

Canonical Section 123 gives the exact finite identity

\[
\boxed{
J_{\rm aug}=2(e_{BB}-k).
}
\tag{IA.1}
\]

Let `R_4` be the number of global bounded strict-rhombus faces, `f` the number of
global bounded nonquadrilateral faces, and `q=|B|`. Then every finite post-ZF C-II
source satisfies

\[
\boxed{
(q-k)+J_{\rm aug}\ge2\sqrt{R_4}.
}
\tag{IA.2}
\]

## 1. Finite proof

Canonical Section 63 gives

\[
e_{BB}=Q+2k+u_B+c_B,
\]

where all displayed defect terms are nonnegative. Hence

\[
e_{BB}-k=Q+k+u_B+c_B\ge Q.
\]

Every bounded nonquadrilateral face has degree at least five, so

\[
Q\ge f.
\]

Therefore (IA.1) gives

\[
\boxed{J_{\rm aug}\ge2f.}
\tag{IA.3}
\]

Canonical Section 85 gives the finite interface inequality

\[
\boxed{q-k+2f\ge2\sqrt{R_4}.}
\tag{IA.4}
\]

Combining (IA.3) and (IA.4) proves (IA.2). No local/global boundary occurrence
identification is used.

## 2. Type-II split

In the canonical full-core Type-II branch,

\[
{R_4\over D^2}\to
\Delta:=\frac\pi{2\sqrt3}.
\]

Thus

\[
\boxed{
\liminf_{D\to\infty}
{(q-k)+J_{\rm aug}\over D}
\ge2\sqrt\Delta
=2\sqrt{\frac\pi{2\sqrt3}}.
}
\tag{IA.5}
\]

The defect term must remain explicit. In particular,

\[
J_{\rm aug}=o(D)
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
\liminf{q-k\over D}\ge2\sqrt\Delta.
\tag{IA.6}
\]

More generally, for fixed `eta>0`, if along a Type-II subsequence

\[
{q-k\over D}\le2\sqrt\Delta-\eta+o(1),
\]

then

\[
\boxed{
J_{\rm aug}\ge(\eta-o(1))D.
}
\tag{IA.7}
\]

This is a dichotomy, not an unconditional `q-k` floor. The recently rejected
`1.9046...` standalone loaded-hull floor must not be inferred from (IA.5) unless the
augmented defect is known to be sublinear.

## 3. Hostile-audit checks

The following points were recomputed independently.

- (IA.1) is exactly the Section-123 identity
  `e_BB-k = (1/2) sum_r(a_r-T_r+Q_r^+) + d_tile`.
- `e_BB-k>=Q>=f` follows from canonical Section 63 and the degree-at-least-five
  property of each bounded nonquadrilateral face.
- The factor `2` in `J_aug>=2f` is correct.
- Substituting into canonical Section 85 preserves the inequality direction.
- The Type-II passage uses only the canonical rhombus-density limit.
- No source point is removed and no affine-kernel statement is extended to
  contact-isolated coordinates.

## 4. Scope

The result does not bound `J_aug` from above and does not eliminate either branch of
the split. It does not address the macroscopic inactive-container branch. It is safe
as a research dependency but is not a theorem-state promotion.

**Verdict:** PASS at audited-working scope. C-II remains open.